cope="col">Case</th><th scope="col">Served</th><th scope="col">Unserved</th><th scope="col">Curtailed</th><th scope="col">Modeled loss</th><th scope="col">Final stored</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Flat supply, no storage</th><td>24</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Block supply, no storage</th><td>12</td><td>12</td><td>12</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Ideal storage</th><td>24</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">80% round-trip case</th><td>21.6</td><td>2.4</td><td>0</td><td>2.4</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Smaller energy account</th><td>18</td><td>6</td><td>6</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Slower charge input</th><td>16.8</td><td>7.2</td><td>6</td><td>1.2</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Slower discharge output</th><td>18</td><td>6</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Supply arrives last</th><td>12</td><td>12</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>12</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="scope"><h2>A defined account, with defined limits</h2><p>The stored balance is output-equivalent deliverable energy. An input c adds eta×c to that account; output d removes d. The toy books (1−eta)×c as modeled conversion loss on entry. It does not time where physical heat is produced or reproduce a real battery’s nameplate capacity.</p><p>The 100% case is an ideal mathematical illustration. The 80% parameter is stipulated, not a measured fleet average. Carryout remains visible: the slow-discharge case ends with 6 MWh stored, while the late-supply case ends with 12 MWh and still leaves 12 MWh unserved earlier in the window.</p><p>This isolated, fixed-window calculation has no weather trace, grid imports, costs, generator ranking, outage process or sub-hour reliability result. No system purchase or plant-design conclusion follows from it.</p><p>Values are displayed to at most three decimals. Full hourly accounting is inspectable below.